#kubectl get pods -n test 
get an error
this is because Roll and RollBinding are namespaced meaning the user will be having permisions only for the namespace where Role binding is defined if we try to access resouces in anotehr namesapce 
we will get an error 
so previously we define the role binding in the default namespace but we are tryying to access the resources from the test namespace in which we did not create the role Binding 

so when we have multiple namespaces defining RoleBinding in every namespace is a TDS Process and Few resources like Persistent volumes are not even namespaced for which we cannot add role binding
there must be a way to define Roles and RoleBindings at the cluster level instead of namespace level that's where cluster Role and Cluster Role Biinding comes into the pictire 
the only difference b/w Role binding and cluster role binding is that RoleBinding is namespaced whereas Cluster RoleBinding is at the Cluster level that means they can access the resources in any namespace 

How to handle 100 of users in the cluster 
should we give same permisions to all users by giving in this array again it's TDS Process rhat's where groups comes into the picture 
Group is nothing but the group of users instead of defining each user seperatly we assign a user to the group and here we give the group instead of giving the user 

